# Call-site ledger of marshmallow at a38b7f6842042e65fd1a485ed152ca99f87880c0.
# Decide every `undecided` line; see macro-benchmark/README.md.
#
# The scope rules A, B1-B5 and C are in macro-benchmark/README.md;
# marshmallow.md shows how this ledger applies them. Fields: the concrete
# package field classes are every public class of fields.py except the
# abstract Number, Mapping and the private _TemporalField; a Field receiver
# without a narrower type dispatches over all of them (marshmallow.md,
# "Dispatch sets"). OrderedSet (Schema.set_class) reaches the only and
# exclude options, because Nested.schema passes OrderedSets there; it is not
# a value of load_only, dump_only, partial or schemes (lead, B2: the
# abstract AbstractSet of types.StrSequenceOrSet names a package class only
# where the package implements it for that role). `missing` is the single
# _Missing instance.
default reject marshmallow.orderedset.OrderedSet.__eq__: no operand of a comparison or `in` test, no element that `in`, set() or a builtin compares, and no dict key in the package is an OrderedSet; OrderedSet defines __eq__ without __hash__, so it is unhashable and is never a key or set element; the compared values are strs, bools, ints, None, tags, unknown options, field names, error messages and client data
default reject marshmallow.orderedset.OrderedSet.__iter__: the iterated, unpacked or converted value at this site is not an OrderedSet: it is a tuple, list, dict, dict view, builtin set, str, generator, mappingproxy, enum class, the client's data or a client iterable typed with the abstract Iterable (B3); an `in` test calls __contains__, which OrderedSet defines, never __iter__; the OrderedSet sites (the only and exclude options, Schema._init_fields and OrderedSet's own methods) accept the candidate explicitly
default reject marshmallow.orderedset.OrderedSet.__len__: the value that this site tests for truth or measures is not an OrderedSet: it is a bool, str, int, None, list, tuple, dict, builtin set, Field, Schema, class, function, regex match or client data; the OrderedSet sites accept the candidate explicitly
default reject marshmallow.orderedset.OrderedSet.__contains__: the right operand of this `in` test is a str, dict, list, tuple, builtin set, mapping or client iterable, not an OrderedSet; only OrderedSet's own methods use `in` on an OrderedSet, through collections.abc (no candidate site)
default reject marshmallow.constants._Missing.__bool__: the package never tests `missing` for truth: it compares it with `is` (fields.py:297, 321, 324, 369; schema.py:542, 652, 687, 1157, 1171), stores it as a default (load_default, dump_default, get_value's default) and returns it from Method._serialize; no truth test, `and`, `or`, `not`, any(), all() or bool() in the package operates on it
default reject marshmallow.constants._Missing.__len__: `missing` reaches no len(), list(), tuple() or truth test at this site; the Length.__call__ test at validate.py:431 receives it only through an opaque client callback result and rejects the candidate explicitly (B5); _Missing defines __bool__, so a truth test of missing would call __bool__, not __len__
default reject marshmallow.constants._Missing.__repr__, marshmallow.fields.Field.__repr__, marshmallow.orderedset.OrderedSet.__repr__, marshmallow.schema.Schema.__repr__, marshmallow.validate.Validator.__repr__: the value that this f-string field formats is a str, bool, int, None, class, class name, re.Pattern, dict or list of messages, or a client value (the input of a field or validator, a client's comparable, bound, choice or attribute), not a package object with __repr__; the fields that format a package object (Field.__repr__, And._repr_args, Schema._init_fields) accept their candidates explicitly

